🧾 AI Finance Tools — Bank Statement Transaction Extractor

An AI-powered tool that reads a bank statement PDF, automatically extracts every transaction using "Google Gemini AI", and exports clean, structured data into a ready-to-use CSV file.

Built by a finance/auditing professional transitioning into AI/ML — this project sits at the intersection of "finance domain knowledge" and "practical AI application", a combination most developers don't have.



🚀 What This Project Does

Manually reading bank statement PDFs and typing transactions into Excel is slow and error-prone. This tool automates that entire process:

1. "Reads" a bank statement PDF (`sample_statement.pdf`)
2. "Extracts" raw text from the PDF using `pdfplumber`
3. "Sends" that text to Google's Gemini AI with a prompt asking it to identify transactions
4. "Receives" clean, structured data back as JSON — with `date`, `description`, `amount`, and `balance` for every transaction
5. "Exports" the final result as a `transactions.csv` file, ready to open in Excel or import into any accounting/analysis tool

"In short:" PDF in → Clean spreadsheet out. No manual typing.


 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| "Python 3.14" | Core programming language |
| "Google Gemini API" | AI model that reads and understands the statement text |
| "pdfplumber" | Extracts raw text from PDF files |
| "pandas" | Converts structured data into a CSV file |
| "python-dotenv" | Keeps the API key safe and out of the code |



 📂 Project Structure


ai-finance-tools/
├── extract_pdf.py          # Main script: PDF → AI → CSV
├── test.py                 # Simple script to test Gemini API connection
├── sample_statement.pdf     # Sample bank statement used for testing
├── transactions.csv        # Output file (generated after running the script)
├── .env                     # Stores API key (NOT uploaded to GitHub — kept private)
├── .gitignore               # Tells Git to ignore .env and other private files
└── README.md                 # This file
```



 ⚙️ How to Run This Project

 1. Clone the repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/chinnadabbadimeghana-max/ai-finance-tools.git
cd ai-finance-tools
```

### 2. Install the required packages
```bash
pip install google-generativeai pdfplumber pandas python-dotenv
```

### 3. Add your own Gemini API key
Create a `.env` file in the project folder with this line:
```
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```
(Get a free API key from [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/))

### 4. Run the script
```bash
python extract_pdf.py
```

5. Check the output
A file named `transactions.csv` will be created in the same folder — open it in Excel to see all extracted transactions.



 💡 Why This Project Matters

Finance and accounting teams spend hours manually processing bank statements, invoices, and financial documents. This project demonstrates how AI can automate that work reliably — combining:

- "Domain expertise" (understanding what a real bank statement looks like, what fields matter for reconciliation/auditing)
- "AI engneering" (prompt design, structured JSON output, API integration)
- "Practical automation" (turning unstructured PDF data into usable business data)



